===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The quality or state of being [[sensitive]]; [[sensitiveness]].
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2019|author=Li Huang; James Lambert|title=Another Arrow for the Quiver: A New Methodology for Multilingual Researchers|journal=Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development|doi=10.1080/01434632.2019.1596115|page=3|text=In any event, the incident, and the media attention it attracted, highlights the '''sensitivity''' of language politics in Singapore and is reflective of the fact that this '''sensitivity''' extends to campus life.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 February 9|author=Tom Allett|title=The BTP's eyes and ears in the air|journal=RAIL|issue=950|page=50|text=Owing to '''sensitivities''' about the force's capabilities, Russell is unable to say how many drones BTP has, or where and when they operate. But he does confide that the force works hand in hand with the helicopter service, and its ability to deploy drones is getting quicker.}}
# {{lb|en|biology}} The [[ability]] of an [[organism]] or [[organ]] to [[respond]] to [[external]] [[stimuli]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2013|month=July-August|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/fenella-saunders Fenella Saunders]|magazine=w:American Scientist
|title=[http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/4/tiny-lenses-see-the-big-picture Tiny Lenses See the Big Picture]
|passage=The single-imaging optic of the mammalian eye offers some distinct visual advantages. Such lenses can take in photons from a wide range of angles, increasing light '''sensitivity'''. They also have high spatial resolution, resolving incoming images in minute detail.}}
## {{senseid|en|vulnerability of a pathogen to treatment}} {{lb|en|biology|medicine|of a {{l|en|pathogen}}}} {{l|en|vulnerability|Vulnerability}} to medical treatment: {{synonym of|en|susceptibility|id=vulnerability of a pathogen to treatment}}.
##: <small>Derived terms:</small> {{w|antibiotic sensitivity testing|sensitivity testing}}
# {{lb|en|statistics}} The [[probability]], in a [[binary]] [[classification]] [[test]], of a {{w|true positive}} being correctly identified.
#: {{coord|en|specificity}}
# {{lb|en|electronics}} The [[degree]] of [[response]] of an [[instrument]] to a [[change]] in an [[input]] [[signal]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-06-05|author=Yvonne Gordon|title=Microplastics found in every sample of water taken during Ocean Race|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2023/jun/05/microplastics-found-in-every-sample-of-water-taken-during-ocean-race|passage=Up to 1,884 microplastic particles were found per cubic metre of seawater in some locations, up to 18 times higher than in similar tests during the last Ocean Race, which ended in 2018. Scientists noted that the '''sensitivity''' of their instruments is now higher.}}
# {{lb|en|photography}} The degree of response of a [[film]] etc. to [[light]] of a [[specified]] [[wavelength]].

